\details{
These functions provide readable formula vocabulary for genomic, single-step,
marker-effect, GWAS, and QTL/eQTL models. Called directly they are inert (they
return \code{NULL}); they take meaning only inside an \code{\link[=hsquared]{hsquared()}} formula.
On this held candidate branch, \code{genomic()} routes the narrow Gaussian REML
random-intercept model through the ordinary no-control \code{\link[=hsquared]{hsquared()}} call;
explicit \verb{engine = "julia", target = "genomic"} remains supported.
Recovery-v3 retry 4 completed 576 official fits and 576 independent base-R
recomputations, but exact Julia replay stopped after 455 rows on a one-ULP
endpoint-representation contract defect. The root and seeds are retired and
unadjudicated; D1/D2 never opened. Fresh Retry-5 recovery and the final
Rose/G10 gates are outstanding, so this is not public activation.
\code{single_step()} remains opt-in and experimental.
The reported genomic coefficient is \code{sigma_g2 / (sigma_g2 + sigma_e2)} on
the declared relationship scale, not generally an average marginal
phenotypic-variance fraction or pedigree/population heritability.
Accepted genomic forms are \code{genomic(1 | id, Ginv = Ginv)} or
\code{genomic(1 | id, markers = M)} (GREML, or SNP-BLUP via
\code{target = "snp_blup"}), and \code{single_step(1 | id, Hinv = Hinv)} (a precomputed
inverse) or \code{single_step(1 | id, pedigree = ped, markers = M)} (the engine
constructs \code{H^-1} from the pedigree + genotyped-subset markers via
\code{target = "single_step_construct"}). Adding \code{group} plus supplied \code{Gamma}
fits a supplied-\code{Gamma}, validation-scale \code{H^Gamma} path through
\code{target = "metafounder_single_step"}; \code{Gamma} is supplied, not estimated.
When \code{data} is an \code{\link[=hs_data]{hs_data()}} container that bundles a pedigree and genotypes,
\code{single_step(1 | id)} resolves both from the bundle (the \code{animal(1 | id)}
precedent), so neither \verb{pedigree =} nor \verb{markers =} is required; explicit
arguments override the bundle. The remaining markers (\code{markers()},
\code{marker_scan()}, \code{qtl_scan()}) are still inert syntax reservations that the
parser rejects with a planned-not-implemented message.
